BUNDLED CODE

One Python script is included, scripts/chunk_article.py. It targets Python 3 and imports
only from the standard library (re, sys, zipfile, typing). It makes no network calls,
spawns no child processes, evaluates no dynamic code, and writes only chunk files
alongside the article it is given.

The script reads .docx by treating it as the zip archive it is and extracting paragraph
text and footnotes from the contained XML, so no third-party document library is needed.
The optional track-changes production path described in SKILL.md is the only feature that
requires an outside package (python-docx); it is not exercised by the bundled script.

