DISCLAIMER

Editorial memos produced by this skill are critique of scholarly writing. They are not
legal advice, and characterizations of doctrine, precedent, or citation validity are an
editor's assessment rather than authority.

Citation review checks form, not existence: a correctly formatted citation to a case that
does not exist, or that does not support the proposition asserted, will pass the Bluebook
pass. Verification is the job of the fact-check pass and depends on web search being
available. Authors remain responsible for confirming that every authority cited exists,
says what it is cited for, and remains good law.
